{
  "cell": "opamp_stage1",
  "_comment": [
    "Cell descriptor for layout/bin/compose-cell.py (issue #46). See",
    "layout/opamp_stage1/README.md for the floorplan, matching style and results.",
    "",
    "SCOPE OF THIS INCREMENT: the NMOS input pair XM1/XM2 of",
    "design/netlist/opamp_core.spice (nfet_01v8, W=6.03, L=1.2, nf=1, m=1).",
    "The PMOS mirror XM3/XM4 (W=4.634) is NOT drawn: 4.634 um is not a",
    "multiple of sky130's 0.005 um manufacturing grid, so no DRC-clean drawing",
    "of that exact width exists (README 'Why the PMOS mirror is not here').",
    "",
    "MATCHING: one klt diff_pair block, splits=2 -> a 2x2 common-centroid",
    "cross-quad (row 0: XM1 | XM2, row 1: XM2 | XM1), each device two 3.015 um",
    "units in parallel (2 x 3.015 = 6.03, exactly the netlist W), both units",
    "of one device on opposite diagonals so their centroids coincide.",
    "Enclosed by the generator's own p-tap guard ring (the substrate/body",
    "contact, strapped to vss via TAP_W).",
    "",
    "snap_ports_to_grid_um: the generator reports S/D port centres at the",
    "midpoint of a 3.015 um strip (y=1.5075/5.7425), half a grid step off-grid;",
    "gen-compose would centre its via stacks there and fail *.ongrid.1. The",
    "driver moves each attach point by <= 0.0025 um, inside the same pad.",
    "",
    "fe_masks: front-end masks the klt generators do not draw on sky130, added as",
    "one klt-draw overlay in the diff_pair's own frame (origin 0,0):",
    "  nsdm 93/44 over all four n-diffusions (0.125 um enclosure);",
    "  psdm 94/20 ring over the p-tap guard ring (0.125 um enclosure);",
    "  npc 95/20 over each gate licon (0.1 um enclosure);",
    "  poly 66/20 endcaps, 0.15 um past the diffusion along the full gate",
    "  width at both ends of every gate (sky130 poly.8 is 0.13 um).",
    "klt's curated deck checks none of these (klayout-tools#2934, #2936); the",
    "PDK's Magic drc(full) does -- see layout/bin/magic-signoff.py.",
    "",
    "ROUTING PLANES (one net family per plane where nets must cross):",
    "  metal  (li1)  vss  -- TAP_W west to its pin stub",
    "  metal2 (met1) tail -- two source columns (x=0.21, x=2.65) joined at y=-2.0",
    "  metal3 (met2) d1 (south/east loop) and inn (west/north loop)",
    "  metal4 (met3) d2 (north) and inp (west)",
    "d1/d2 and inn/inp are the cross-quad's two inherently crossing pairs, so",
    "each pair is split across met2/met3.",
    "",
    "PINS: every boundary net ends on a klt-draw stub at the cell edge (west:",
    "tail, inn, vss, inp; east: d1, d2) whose PAD is promoted via pins[]."
  ],
